    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p>If we draw a small circle around the point <m>P</m> we can  see that the flow rate out
is larger than the flow rate in (the vectors exiting the circle are longer than the vectors entering the circle). Thus the divergence is positive.</p>
<p>If we draw a small circle around the point <m>P</m> we can  see that the flow rate out
equals  the flow rate in. Thus the divergence is zero. The vector field is incompressible at the point P.</p>
<p>If we draw a small circle around the point <m>P</m> we can  see that the flow rate out
is smaller than the flow rate in (the vectors exiting the circle are shorter than the vectors entering the circle). Thus the divergence is negative.</p>
</solution>
